{"term":"brim","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:3abcead783f2e76b52","definition":"Originally, a border or edge of a sea, a river, or other body of water; now, any border or edge.","example":"Yet ſtill that direful ſtroke kept on his vvay, / And falling heauie on Cambellos creſt, / Strooke him ſo hugely, that in ſvvovvne he lay, / And in his head an hideous vvound impreſt: / And ſure had it not happily found reſt / Vpon the brim of his brode plated ſhield, / It vvould haue cleft his braine dovvne to his breſt.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b36f4fefd5dfb373be","definition":"To fill (a container) to the brim (noun etymology 1, noun sense 1.1), top, or upper edge.","example":"Arrange the board and brim the glass.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bulge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:92381303cbadbea916","definition":"To fill (something) fully.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":["bulge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:f82f9afaa76f43e530","definition":"To be full until almost overflowing.","example":"The room brimmed with people.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["teem","bulge"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"also, figuratively","register":"also, figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:73a6e70d784a5dc3bf","definition":"The sea; ocean; water; flood.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0816ace5790acd6b92","definition":"Synonym of bream (“a freshwater fish from one of a number of genera”); specifically (US), the redbreast sunfish (Lepomis auritus).","example":"Sometimes her daddy would take her fishing for catfish or brim (bream) out on the lake in his john boat.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["bream"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Australia, US","register":"Australia, US","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8e8d21b8d3cf4f1728","definition":"Of a boar (“male pig”): to mate with (a sow (“female pig”)); to rut.","example":"Svvine alone of all creatures vvhen they be brimming, froth and fome at the mouth. And as for the Bore, if he heare the grunting of a Sovv that ſeekes to be brimmed, unleſſe he may come to her, vvill forſake his meat, untill he be leane and poore: and ſhe againe vvill be ſo farre enraged, that ſhe vvill be readie to run upon a man and all to teare him, eſpecially if his cloths be vvhite.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, transitive","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:068bd93a3d768f464e","definition":"Of a sow: to be in heat; to rut; also, to mate with a boar.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"archaic","register":"archaic, intransitive","wordFamily":["abrim","brimful","brimfully","brimless","brimmy","broadbrim","halo brim","hatbrim","overbrim","snapbrim","to the brim","underbrim","brimmed","brimmer","brimming","brim over"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brim#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6fbe254a335b068385","definition":"The period when a sow (“female pig”) is ready to mate; a heat, an oestrus, a rut; also, an act of a boar (“male pig”) and sow mating.","example":"You ſhall ſay […] Boare […] goeth to his […] Brymme.","pos":"noun","s